==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[sherd]]

===Etymology===
From {{ME.}} < {{OE.}} ''[[sceard]]''.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|dab=Shard}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[piece]] of [[broken]] [[glass]] or [[pottery]], especially one found in an [[archaeological]] [[dig]].
# A piece of material, especially rock and similar materials, reminding of a broken piece of glass or pottery.
# A tough [[scale]], [[sheath]], or [[shell]]; it is especially used as a term to refer to the [[elytra]] of a beetle.
# {{context|online role-playing}} An [[instance]] of an [[MMORPG]] that is one of several independent and structurally identical [[virtual]] worlds, none of which has so many players as to exhaust a system's [[resource]]s.

====Derived terms====
* [[potsherd]]

